    <para id="para-00041">Gunter, K. B., Almstedt, H. C., &amp; Janz, K. F. (2012). Physical activity in childhood may be the key to optimizing lifespan skeletal health. <emphasis effect="italics">Exercise and Sport Sciences Reviews, 40</emphasis>(1), 13. https://doi.org/10.1097/JES.0b013e318236e5ee</para>
    <para id="para-00042">Heath, G. W., &amp; Levine, D. (2022). Physical activity and public health among people with disabilities: Research gaps and recommendations. <emphasis effect="italics">International Journal of Environmental Research and Public Health, 19</emphasis>(16), 10436. https://doi.org/10.3390/ijerph191610436</para>
    <para id="para-00043">Johnson, K., Caskey, M., Rand, K., Tucker, R., &amp; Vohr, B. (2014). Gender differences in adult-infant communication in the first months of life. <emphasis effect="italics">Pediatrics, 134</emphasis>(6), 1603–1610. https://doi.org/10.1542/peds.2013-4289</para>
    <para id="para-00044">Kokštejn, J., Musálek, M., &amp; Tufano, J. J. (2017). Are sex differences in fundamental motor skills uniform throughout the entire preschool period? <emphasis effect="italics">PLoS ONE, 12</emphasis>(4). https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0176556</para>
